VTID-03788 — commands.log
==========================

## Discovery

After PR #3226 (VTID-03787) merged (sha 4a88b1dc), sampled staging
build-info 20x over ~60s — every sample still reported the PRE-merge
commit 005cd4be.

$ (via GitHub Actions MCP) list_workflow_runs AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml
-> last 5 runs: 4 consecutive "failure" (7370c289, e174d85a, 2ba5d7bf,
   4a88b1dc), then "success" for the prior commit 005cd4be.

$ (via GitHub Actions MCP) list_workflow_jobs for run 33174044946 (the
  4a88b1dc merge-commit run)
-> {"jobs":{"total_count":0,"jobs":[]}}
   Same result for the very first run (33172965619, commit 7370c289).
   0 jobs = failed before any job step executed.

## Root-cause isolation

Extracted the "Register task-definition revision + roll the service"
step's `run: |` script (the block from `NEW_DEF=$(aws ecs
describe-task-definition` through `echo "Service stable on $NEW_ARN"`)
via a small python script, stripped YAML indentation, wrote to
/tmp/extracted_step.sh, ran:

$ bash -n /tmp/extracted_step.sh
/tmp/extracted_step.sh: line 87: syntax error near unexpected token `|'
/tmp/extracted_step.sh: line 87: `      | .containerDefinitions[0].secrets |='

Read the surrounding jq program (lines ~443-536 of the workflow file) —
confirmed my own VTID-03787 comment block (added for
ORB_LOG_NOVA_INSTRUCTION_DEBUG) lived INSIDE the single-quoted jq
program passed to `jq`, and contained the text "the user's memory and
personalization context" — the apostrophe in "user's" closes the
enclosing bash single-quote early.

Confirmed this is a known, previously-hit defect class: lines 434-441 of
the SAME file (pre-existing, from an earlier VTID) explicitly document an
identical incident and instruct that jq-program comments must live
OUTSIDE the single-quoted string, specifically to avoid this. My comment
violated that documented rule.

## Fix

Edited .github/workflows/AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml — reworded the
ORB_LOG_NOVA_INSTRUCTION_DEBUG comment to remove the apostrophe ("the
user's" -> "real user"), and added an explicit line-item warning inside
the comment itself flagging this as the second incident of the class.

$ bash -n /tmp/extracted_step2.sh   (re-extracted after the fix)
(clean, exit 0)

## New regression test

Added services/gateway/test/orb/live/upstream/staging-deploy-workflow-bash-syntax.test.ts
— parses both AWS-STAGE-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml and AWS-PROD-DEPLOY-GATEWAY.yml
with js-yaml, extracts every job's every `run:` step, shells each out to
`bash -n`, plus a narrower test isolating the task-def-update step's jq
program and asserting no apostrophe survives in it.

$ npx jest test/orb/live/upstream/staging-deploy-workflow-bash-syntax.test.ts
PASS — 5/5

## Mutation verification

Reintroduced the exact bug (swapped "real user" back to "the user's") in
the live workflow file, re-ran:

$ npx jest test/orb/live/upstream/staging-deploy-workflow-bash-syntax.test.ts
FAIL — 2/5 (the bash -n step test + the apostrophe-absence test), 3/5
       still passing (PROD workflow tests + sanity checks, correctly
       unaffected by a STAGE-only mutation)

Restored from /tmp/stage-workflow.bak, diffed clean (RESTORED_CLEAN),
re-ran:

$ npx jest test/orb/live/upstream/staging-deploy-workflow-bash-syntax.test.ts
PASS — 5/5

